export default "import { Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\n\n<Meta title=\"Docs/A2UI Control Surface\" />\n\n# A2UI Control Surface — Foundation Layer\n\n> *Wire the AI to fully control all three columns. Not a chatbot. A surface controller.*\n\n**Status: 🔄 Phase 1–2 complete, Phase 3–4 planned**\n\n---\n\n## The Vision\n\nAI controls all three columns. XML tags inject content into sections. Section CRUD is done. Session-scoped conversations are wired. AI-driven tab switching, RUN triggering, and element-level ID tracking are active.\n\nThe AI is not a passive chat widget — it is the primary interface for modifying the workspace. It reads context, writes to sections, navigates tabs, triggers execution, evaluates output, and will soon iterate autonomously.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Session-Scoped Chat ✅\n\nEach prompt session owns its conversation. Opening a prompt loads **its** chat history — not the global most-recent conversation.\n\n- `handleLoadPromptSession` passes `conversationId` to InteractiveChatInterface\n- InteractiveChatInterface accepts `initialConversationId` prop, auto-loads on mount\n- On prompt switch: saves current chat state, loads new session's conversation\n\n**Relevant files:**\n- `frontend/src/pages/WritingAreaIndex.tsx` — Session loading, conversation scoping\n- `frontend/src/components/InteractiveChatInterface.tsx` — Chat, tabs, tag processing\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: AI Control Tags ✅\n\nThe AI navigates and executes through XML command tags intercepted by the frontend and executed on the DOM.\n\n### Section Control Tags\n\n| Tag | Action |\n|-----|--------|\n| `<update_agent>text</update_agent>` | Write to System Role |\n| `<update_user>text</update_user>` | Write to User Role |\n| `<update_tool>text</update_tool>` | Write to Tool Call |\n| `<update_few_shot>text</update_few_shot>` | Write to Few Shot |\n| `<update_context>text</update_context>` | Write to Context |\n| `<update_constraints>text</update_constraints>` | Write to Constraints |\n| `<add_role name=\"X\">content</add_role>` | Create custom section |\n| `<remove_role name=\"X\"/>` | Remove section |\n\n### Navigation & Execution Tags\n\n| Tag | Action |\n|-----|--------|\n| `<switch_tab>trace\\|variables\\|chat</switch_tab>` | Switch right-column tab |\n| `<run_prompt/>` | Trigger prompt execution |\n| `<show_version>N</show_version>` | Load version in variables tab |\n| `<eval_grounding/>` | Evaluate output against grounding metrics |\n| `<save/>` `<get_versions/>` `<load_version>N` | Milvus memory operations |\n\n### How It Works\n\nTags are stripped from the visible chat by a frontend interceptor in `InteractiveChatInterface.tsx`. The interceptor pattern-matches XML tags, extracts content, and dispatches actions:\n\n1. Section update tags → `ResponsivePromptBuilder` receives content via state\n2. `<add_role>`, `<remove_role>` → Custom events (`add-prompt-role`, `remove-prompt-role`) listened by `PromptWorkspace`\n3. `<switch_tab>` → `selectedNav` state change\n4. `<run_prompt/>` → Custom event `ai-run-prompt` listened by `PromptWorkspace`\n5. `<eval_grounding/>` → Grounding metrics panel renders in Trace tab\n\nTags are never shown to the user. The AI also renders clickable action buttons: `[Confirm](action:confirm)`, `[Remove \"Section\"](action:remove_role:Section)`.\n\n**Relevant files:**\n- `frontend/src/components/InteractiveChatInterface.tsx` — Tag processing, chat rendering\n- `frontend/src/components/PromptWorkspace.tsx` — Section CRUD listeners, RUN listener\n- `backend/grace_gui.py` — Tag interception and processing\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Element ID Layer 🔄\n\nEvery DOM element the AI touches gets a stable UUID attribute:\n\n- `data-section-id` on every prompt section\n- `data-run-id` on every execution output\n- IDs persist across saves in `prompt_sessions.left_column_content` JSON\n- Trace tab tracks changes **per ID**, not per text block\n\n**Why this matters:** Without stable IDs, the trace sees \"text changed from X to Y.\" With IDs, it sees \"Section #constraints-7a3b: line 3 changed, line 7 added.\" The trace becomes a structured audit log, not a diff dump.\n\n**Status:** Not started. Infrastructure prerequisite for Phase 4.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Autonomous Loop 🔜\n\nThe AI iterates without user intervention:\n\n1. User or AI sets target: `<loop_target>groundedness:0.9</loop_target>`\n2. AI triggers RUN\n3. Output is evaluated against grounding metrics (faithfulness, hallucination, recall, relevance, completeness)\n4. If score < target: AI edits the relevant section, re-runs\n5. Loop continues until convergence\n6. On convergence: AI posts a notification message, stops looping\n\n**Safety constraints:**\n- Max iterations configurable (default: 5)\n- User can interrupt at any time\n- Each iteration is versioned\n- Convergence notification includes iteration count and final scores\n\n**Status:** Not started. Depends on Phase 3 (element IDs) and grounding metrics pipeline.\n\n---\n\n## Grounding Metrics (Active in Trace Tab)\n\nThe Trace tab displays five evaluation dimensions:\n\n| Metric | What It Measures |\n|--------|-----------------|\n| **Faithfulness** | Does the output stay true to the source material? |\n| **Hallucination** | Are there fabricated claims not in the input? |\n| **Recall** | Did it capture all relevant information? |\n| **Relevance** | Is every sentence relevant to the query? |\n| **Completeness** | Did it answer all parts of the question? |\n\nEach metric renders as a progress bar with score. A \"Healthy / Drifting\" toggle warns when any metric drops below threshold. The panel is rendered in the Trace tab via `groundingMetrics` state in `InteractiveChatInterface.tsx`.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n- [x] AI says \"add a Constraints section\" → section appears in left column\n- [x] AI says \"switch to trace tab\" → trace tab opens\n- [x] AI says \"run the prompt\" → output appears in third column\n- [x] Open prompt → its chat history loads via `conversation_id` linkage *(2026-07-15)*\n- [ ] AI sets loop target → iterates until threshold met\n- [ ] Trace tab shows per-element change history\n\n---\n\n## Relevant Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `frontend/src/components/PromptWorkspace.tsx` | Section CRUD listeners, `sessionId` → `InteractiveChatInterface` |\n| `frontend/src/components/InteractiveChatInterface.tsx` | Chat, tabs, tag processing, session-scoped conversation loading |\n| `frontend/src/pages/WritingAreaIndex.tsx` | Session loading, `handleConversationChange` → DB persistence |\n| `backend/main.py` | API routes, `UpdatePromptSessionRequest` with `conversation_id` |\n| `backend/prompt_sessions_api.py` | Session CRUD, UUID validation, `conversation_id` update |\n| `frontend/src/services/conversationStorage.ts` | API-first conversation CRUD, Sentry-monitored |\n"